  "conclusion": "Replication passed: the deployed config refit on the ablation split scores 0.5622 against 0.5622 in ablation_results.json, on a training matrix bit-identical to ablate_voice's. Across the 54-config grid (GroupKFold(5) over training speakers only), CV macro-F1 runs from 0.5402 to 0.5612 (median 0.5514). The deployed config scores 0.5496 +/- 0.0180 and ranks 29/54. max_leaf_nodes moves the marginal mean most (0.0105), yet every hyperparameter's marginal range, that one included, is smaller than one fold-std of the deployed config (0.0180). Early stopping is active, so the deployed model uses 100 of its 300-iteration cap and max_iter is not the binding setting. Early stopping itself was held at its deployed value (ON); a CV-only row with it OFF scores 0.5625 +/- 0.0070, above the CV-best 0.5612, but it was never a selection candidate, so the test set says nothing about it. On the fixed test set, the CV-best config (learning_rate=0.03, max_iter=300, max_leaf_nodes=63, l2_regularization=1.0; 219 iterations) scores 0.5644 against 0.5622 for the deployed config: a paired difference of +0.0021, 95% CI [-0.0117, +0.0154], with the best config ahead in 62.7% of resamples. No detectable gain: the CI includes 0, so the hand-set values of the searched hyperparameters cost no measurable accuracy and the deployed model stays as it is.",
